Thank you for providing additional clarification. Concurrent works refer to those that have NOT been published in conferences or journals with peer review at the time the authors submit their paper. LogitNorm is released on arXiv in May and demonstrated at ICML in July, whereas the submission deadline for ICLR is in September. Therefore, *being a concurrent work* is unjustified.

You can use your own discretion to determine whether or not this constitutes plagiarism:

- The authors admit that they know the work of LogitNorm when they worked on LogitClip;

- The authors (and other reviewers) agree that LogitNorm is an important related work w.r.t. LogitClip;

- The authors neither cited nor discussed LogitNorm in their submitted paper.
